<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch Sept CPI seen up at 2.0 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch Sept CPI seen up at 2.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters predict the official September Dutch consumer price index (CPI), due Friday, to rise around 0.9 percent from August, giving a 2.0-percent year-on-year rise. Seasonal factors like end of summer sales and tuition fee payments were cited for rise.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT   Date Period   Indicator	   Consensus  Range     Pvs</p>
<p> 0830  11/10 September CPI Y/Y change   2.0 pct    1.9-2.1  1.9</p>
<p> 0830  11/10 September CPI M/M change   0.9 pct    0.8-1.0 -0.1</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
